"""Editorial question designs for three home-living niches."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


SUSTAINABLE = """history_origins|A Household Practice Changes|Which dated policy or technology altered a particular home's resource use?|Compare records before and after; avoid a single origin story.
famous_examples|A Low-Impact Home Claim Tested|Which measured outcome supports a named household practice?|State baseline, boundary, period, and comparison.
hidden_stories|Labor behind a Green Routine|Whose time, money, or public infrastructure makes a practice possible?|Include household and service-provider accounts.
beginner_explainers|What Is Being Reduced?|Does a change target energy, material use, water, waste, or cost?|Define metric and full life-cycle boundary.
advanced_concepts|Tradeoffs across Impacts|Does reducing one impact raise another elsewhere in the life cycle?|Compare quantified alternatives with uncertainty.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Unverified Eco Claim|Which data are missing to assess a product or habit?|Name functional unit, baseline, and measurement method.
technology_innovation|A Home Efficiency Device|What measured change follows its installation in one setting?|Compare meter data, weather, occupancy, and costs.
people_personalities|A Household Changes a Habit|Which constraint led to a documented sustainable choice?|Use consented interviews and actual bills or logs.
major_events|A Local Program Begins|What changed after an energy, waste, or water policy took effect?|Check eligibility, participation, and measured outcomes.
how_it_works|Following a Product's Life|Where do extraction, production, use, and disposal impacts arise?|Define product, functional unit, and geography.
rise_fall|A Green Product Reassessed|Which evidence challenged an earlier environmental claim?|Compare dated assessments and their boundaries.
then_vs_now|One Household over Time|Did measured consumption change after an intervention?|Normalize for household, weather, and service level.
future_developments|A Conditional Home Upgrade|Which assumptions control projected savings or impacts?|Show scenario range and upfront burden.
myths_vs_facts|Recyclable Means Recycled?|What local collection and processing actually happen to a material?|Trace accepted items and downstream route.
documentary_stories|A Home Resource Audit|How did measurement change a household's priorities?|Follow baseline, intervention, and follow-up evidence.
lived_experience|Living with a New Routine|What time, comfort, or access burdens accompany an impact reduction?|Use dated logs and consented accounts.
institutional_pathway|Who Enables the Change?|Which landlord, utility, council, or provider decision matters?|Map actual approval and service pathway.
incentives_norms|Why Households Adopt It|How do price, norms, convenience, and eligibility shape uptake?|Use bounded evidence, not assumed motives.
access_and_exclusion|Who Cannot Make This Choice?|Which capital, tenure, mobility, or infrastructure barrier excludes households?|Identify affected groups and feasible alternatives.
community_variation|Different Homes, Different Results|How do climate, building, and household size alter performance?|Compare matched metrics across settings.
policy_in_practice|A Sustainability Rule in Use|Did a local program deliver its stated benefits?|Compare policy text, uptake, and measured outcomes.
survey_vs_story|What Self-Reports Miss|Do stated green habits match purchase, meter, or waste records?|Check consent, sample, and measurement gaps.
power_and_voice|Who Sets the Green Standard?|Whose needs and costs shape a housing or waste policy?|Trace decision records and affected resident input.
unintended_consequence|A Rebound after Savings|Did lower cost or added convenience increase other consumption?|Use before-and-after totals, not just unit efficiency.
comparative_setting|Two Ways to Meet One Need|Which option has lower impact for an identical service?|Set common functional unit and local conditions.
change_over_time|Does the Benefit Last?|How do repairs, behavior, and equipment age change results?|Measure beyond initial adoption.
ethical_dilemma|Low Impact versus Affordability|Who pays and who benefits from a proposed household change?|Show tradeoffs and distribution, not a single moral ranking.
field_space_constraints|A Sustainability Measure in a Real Home|Does site area or shared space permit it?|Measure roof, storage, access, or garden constraints.
field_household_cost|Upfront and Running Cost|What does installation, upkeep, finance, and disposal cost?|Use dated local prices and ranges.
field_design_for_access|Usable for Every Resident?|Does a new system create physical or information barriers?|Test with named users and alternatives.
field_maintenance_burden|Keeping Savings Real|What cleaning, repair, or calibration does a system need?|Check manuals and actual upkeep logs.
field_material_lifecycle|Full Material Footprint|What extraction, use, reuse, and end-of-life impacts are counted?|State boundary, data source, and uncertainty.
"""

ORGANIZATION = """history_origins|A Household Storage Practice|Which dated housing or work change shaped a storage norm?|Use plans, catalogs, and household accounts.
famous_examples|A Room That Stays Usable|What evidence shows an organizing system works after daily use?|Compare before, after, and follow-up with the same tasks.
hidden_stories|The Labor of Order|Who sorts, cleans, labels, and resets a household system?|Record time and unequal task distribution.
beginner_explainers|Organize for a Task|How can items be placed so a specific activity is easier?|Define user, frequency, reach, and retrieval time.
advanced_concepts|Storage versus Behavior|Does adding containers solve a capacity problem or just hide it?|Measure inventory, space, and repeated use.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why Does Clutter Return?|Which capacity or routine gap can observation distinguish?|Use a consented household log rather than diagnosis.
technology_innovation|A Digital Inventory at Home|Does a label or app improve retrieval enough to justify upkeep?|Compare task time, errors, and maintenance.
people_personalities|A Household Negotiates Space|Whose preferences changed a shared storage plan?|Use consented accounts without assigning blame.
major_events|A Move Forces Reorganization|Which possessions and routines changed after relocation?|Compare inventory and use across dated homes.
how_it_works|From Inventory to Placement|How does a household decide what belongs where?|Trace actual tasks, dimensions, ownership, and agreement.
rise_fall|An Organizing Trend Reconsidered|Why did a once-popular container or rule stop working?|Use long-term use evidence and costs.
then_vs_now|A Storage System after Six Months|Which retrieval, safety, or upkeep outcomes changed?|Use same measures before and after.
future_developments|Planning for a New Need|How can a system adapt when work, care, or household size changes?|Present adjustable scenarios, not a perfect solution.
myths_vs_facts|Tidying Takes One Day?|What continued labor does a photo-ready makeover omit?|Record maintenance over a defined period.
documentary_stories|One Home's Organization Trial|What did a household try, revise, and retain?|Follow dated inventory, layout, and resident feedback.
lived_experience|Finding Things in Daily Life|Which tasks became faster or harder after reorganization?|Use participant logs and specific tasks.
institutional_pathway|Rules in Shared Housing|Which lease, building, or workplace rule limits storage choices?|Read actual policy and approval process.
incentives_norms|What Counts as Order?|How do aesthetics, time, and shared expectations shape a system?|Ask users before imposing a standard.
access_and_exclusion|Storage within Reach|Who cannot access a shelf, label, or digital inventory?|Test with named users and alternatives.
community_variation|Different Homes, Different Order|How do family size, routines, and cultural practices affect storage?|Compare situated examples without moral ranking.
policy_in_practice|A Shared-Space Rule|Does a building's storage policy work as stated?|Compare rule with resident use and complaints.
survey_vs_story|A Satisfaction Score after Tidying|Does a survey reflect retrieval time and maintenance labor?|Compare self-report with observed tasks.
power_and_voice|Whose Belongings Move?|Who decides what is kept, displayed, or discarded in shared space?|Track consent and ownership.
unintended_consequence|More Containers, More Work|Did new storage increase purchases or reset time?|Compare inventory, costs, and household labor.
comparative_setting|Two Layouts for One Task|Which arrangement reduces steps or reach for a user?|Measure under comparable conditions.
change_over_time|An Organizing System Ages|What happens when inventory or household routines shift?|Follow the same system across months.
ethical_dilemma|Decluttering Another Person's Items|How are privacy, consent, and shared safety balanced?|Use explicit agreements and avoid unilateral disposal.
field_space_constraints|Storage within a Floor Plan|Can cabinets and containers fit without blocking circulation?|Measure actual room and access route.
field_household_cost|Price of the System|What do shelving, containers, labels, and replacement add?|Use itemized dated costs.
field_design_for_access|Retrieval for Different Users|Can intended users see, reach, and return items independently?|Test actual tasks and formats.
field_maintenance_burden|How Much Reset Work?|Who returns items and how often?|Log time and identify failure points.
field_material_lifecycle|The Container's Own Footprint|Does new storage require more material than it saves?|Compare reuse, durability, and disposal.
"""

MINIMALISM = """history_origins|A Simplicity Movement in Context|Which dated social or artistic practice shaped a named minimalist approach?|Attribute the specific tradition and avoid one origin.
famous_examples|A Minimal Home in Use|What does a photographed sparse home reveal and conceal about daily life?|Compare inventory, storage, and occupant accounts.
hidden_stories|The Labor behind Less|Who shops, repairs, rents, stores, or cleans for a minimalist household?|Trace externalized work and cost.
beginner_explainers|Define Less of What|Does a minimalist practice reduce possessions, purchases, space, or obligations?|Choose a measure before judging results.
advanced_concepts|Less Stuff, Same Service?|Does a low-consumption choice maintain a household's needed function?|Compare functional units and equity effects.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Unmeasured Benefit Claim|Which evidence is missing for a claim about wellbeing or footprint?|Specify comparison group, outcome, and confounders.
technology_innovation|Digital Substitution|Does replacing physical goods with subscriptions reduce cost or impact?|Count devices, energy, fees, and service access.
people_personalities|Why One Household Downsized|What documented changes in need or values led to fewer possessions?|Use consented accounts, not personality diagnosis.
major_events|A Move to Less Space|What changed in purchases, routines, and costs after downsizing?|Compare dated records and household composition.
how_it_works|A Purchase Decision|How does a person decide to keep, borrow, repair, or buy?|Trace actual task and available alternatives.
rise_fall|A Minimalist Rule Abandoned|Which unmet need or hidden cost led to revision?|Use household follow-up, not ideology.
then_vs_now|A Household before and after Decluttering|Which inventory, spending, and use patterns changed?|Measure over time, not just a single photograph.
future_developments|A Low-Consumption Scenario|What could change if access to repair or sharing improves?|State assumptions and distributional effects.
myths_vs_facts|Less Always Greener?|When do travel, replacement, or outsourcing offset fewer possessions?|Use full life-cycle boundary.
documentary_stories|A Year of Keeping Less|How did a household test and revise its own rules?|Follow dated choices, costs, and lived experience.
lived_experience|Living with Fewer Things|Which tasks become easier or harder for a specific household?|Use consented accounts over a defined period.
institutional_pathway|Services that Make Less Possible|Which libraries, rentals, repairs, or public spaces substitute for ownership?|Map access and eligibility.
incentives_norms|Why Minimalism Appeals|Which cost, aesthetic, time, or environmental motive is documented?|Use participants' own words and avoid assumed virtue.
access_and_exclusion|Who Cannot Own Less Easily?|Which disability, caregiving, work, or rural need changes the tradeoff?|Compare actual access and alternatives.
community_variation|Different Forms of Simplicity|How do low-consumption practices vary by household and place?|Avoid treating one lifestyle as universal.
policy_in_practice|Repair and Reuse Services|Did a local program make reduced buying practical?|Compare rules, uptake, and access gaps.
survey_vs_story|Does Minimalism Improve Wellbeing?|What does a self-selected survey show versus household accounts?|State sample, measure, and causal limits.
power_and_voice|Who Chooses to Discard?|Can all household members shape decisions about shared items?|Check consent and ownership.
unintended_consequence|The Hidden Rental or Storage Bill|Did owning less shift cost or labor elsewhere?|Track paid services and trips.
comparative_setting|The Same Rule in Two Homes|How does a reduced-inventory target work under different needs?|Compare function rather than item count alone.
change_over_time|A Minimalist Practice after Years|Do purchasing and replacement patterns remain lower?|Use longitudinal records and changing needs.
ethical_dilemma|Keeping Less and Sharing Burdens|Who bears the cost if a household stops owning a needed item?|Identify affected people and alternatives.
field_space_constraints|Space Saved and Space Borrowed|How much floor area was freed versus off-site storage used?|Measure both locations.
field_household_cost|Cost of Owning Less|Do replacement, rental, delivery, or travel costs offset savings?|Use dated household spending.
field_design_for_access|Necessary Tools for Independence|Which possessions support a resident's access or care?|Ask users and avoid arbitrary item limits.
field_maintenance_burden|Care of Fewer Objects|Did upkeep time fall, or move to shared and rented goods?|Log tasks across a period.
field_material_lifecycle|Consumption beyond Item Count|Do retained goods, services, and disposal have lower total impacts?|Define functional unit and life-cycle data.
"""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("396", "396_sustainable_living", SUSTAINABLE,
                  "Sustainable living as measurable, site-specific changes to household energy, water, materials, waste, and access, evaluated across a stated life cycle.",
                  "EPA life-cycle guidance, meter and utility data, product declarations, local service and policy records, itemized costs, and consented household logs",
                  "Define baseline, functional unit, geography, time, and impact boundary. Avoid universal green labels or guaranteed savings; account for household constraints and shifted burdens.")
    revise_domain("397", "397_organization", ORGANIZATION,
                  "Home organization as the ongoing arrangement of belongings and routines for specific users, tasks, shared decisions, accessibility, cost, and maintenance.",
                  "measured rooms and inventories, consented task observations, household agreements, itemized costs, follow-up logs, and relevant professional ethics",
                  "Do not equate visual tidiness with usability or moral worth. Respect privacy and ownership; avoid diagnosing a person from household clutter.")
    revise_domain("398", "398_minimalism", MINIMALISM,
                  "Minimalism in home living as a set of varied choices about possessions, purchases, space, and services, examined through household needs and actual consequences.",
                  "dated inventories and spending logs, consented resident accounts, access and service records, life-cycle assessments, and original low-consumption research",
                  "Specify what is reduced and for whom. Do not assume fewer objects cause wellbeing or lower environmental impact without a matched comparison and full boundary.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
